79. ACCESSIBILITY

Ensure:

- accessible tables
- keyboard navigation
- accessible confirmation dialog
- clear progress/status
- clear error messages

==================================================
80. PERFORMANCE

Do not:

- generate PDFs in the browser
- send large PDFs through multiple frontend layers
- load all PDFs into memory

Generation belongs on the backend/worker.

==================================================
81. NO AI

Do not introduce:

OpenAI
LLM
RAG
OCR
machine learning

This is deterministic document processing.

==================================================
82. NO CROWDMARK API

Do not upload generated documents to Crowdmark.

Do not synchronize grades.

Do not create Crowdmark submissions.

That is future functionality.

==================================================
83. NO QR CODE YET

Do not add a QR code unless the project's existing requirements already
define the exact payload and destination.

Otherwise defer QR code generation to the next phase.

The document generator should be designed so a QR overlay can be added later
without rewriting the PDF generator.

For example, conceptually:

PDF overlay components:

Student Information
Room/Seat Information
QR Code [future]

Do not implement the QR component yet.

==================================================
84. DOCUMENT DESIGN

Keep the document design professional and conservative.

Avoid:

- large graphics
- decorative elements
- unnecessary colors
- excessive branding

The document must print clearly on normal university printers.

Prioritize:

readability
identity
room/seat visibility
exam content preservation

==================================================
85. PRINT SAFETY

The generated document should have:

reasonable margins
readable text
no clipped text
no overlapping content

Test using actual PDF rendering where possible.

